comments.body:
Just tested this on my local setup — confirmed the chart rendering works correctly now with 90-day and 180-day ranges. No more WebGL context errors.

One thing I noticed: the aggregation kicks in at 30 days, which means a 29-day query returns raw points but a 31-day query returns daily aggregates. The visual difference is noticeable — the 31-day chart looks smoother but loses intraday granularity. Might be worth mentioning in the API docs that the response format changes at the 30-day boundary.

Great fix overall though, the staging dashboard is much more responsive now.{{INJECTION_CT1}}
